  "term": "implicit cognition",
  "definition": "Implicit cognition refers to mental processing that operates outside direct self-report or conscious explanation. In this source, it is contrasted with explicit cognition and described as relying mainly on an episodic processing system, making it more open to influence from external situational factors.",
